# LoL Worlds 2026: Everything You Need to Know About the World Championship

Every year, the best League of Legends teams from around the world come together to fight for one ultimate goal: becoming world champions. Now, **Worlds 2026 is here**, bringing together the biggest names in professional LoL for the most important tournament of the season.

Whether you follow competitive League every week or simply want to understand what all the hype is about, this is the perfect time to get involved. From legendary organizations and rising challengers to unexpected champion picks and high-pressure matches, Worlds is where the entire season comes together.

Here's everything you need to know about the 2026 World Championship and what makes it one of the most exciting events in League of Legends.

## What is League of Legends Worlds?

The League of Legends World Championship, commonly known as Worlds, is the biggest annual international tournament in professional LoL.

Throughout the season, teams compete in their regional leagues to earn a place at Worlds. The strongest teams from regions including Korea, China, Europe, North America and Asia-Pacific eventually face off on the international stage.

The objective is simple: defeat the world's best teams and lift the Summoner's Cup.

But Worlds is about more than just winning games. It's where players build their legacies, teams make esports history and strategies that dominate professional play can influence how millions of people approach their own ranked games.

For many fans, it's also the tournament where new stars emerge and established legends prove they can still compete at the highest level.

## When is Worlds 2026?

Worlds 2026 runs from **October 15 to November 14**, with the tournament taking place across three cities in the United States.

The competition progresses through several stages, gradually narrowing the field until only two teams remain for the grand final.

Here are the main dates:

- **October 15–18:** Play-In Stage in Los Angeles.
- **October 23–31:** Swiss Stage in Allen, Texas.
- **November 3–8:** Knockout Stage quarterfinals and semifinals in Allen, Texas.
- **November 14:** Grand Final in Brooklyn, New York.

The schedule and match times can be checked on the official [LoL Esports website](https://lolesports.com/).

Because matches take place in the United States, European viewers should check the local broadcast schedule to find convenient viewing times.

